# fuse, toolchain llvm
### lib/fuse.c keeps the older versions of its symbols with a .symver in inline assembly, whose target
### name nothing else in the sources uses: LLVM sees no reference to it, drops the definition, and lld
### stops ("default version symbol fuse_session_loop_mt@@FUSE_3.12 must be defined"). gcc keeps it, and
### with clang the library is built without LTO
PKG_OVERRIDELTO=0
